s  and a 7-inch screen for the multimedia  system passengers also get to enjoy the  ride the rav4 has one of the most  spacious cabins in the class  the trunk offers an impressive 547  liters of space or 501 liters in this  hybrid version the additional electric  motor also increases the overall weight  to 1.7 tonnes but those are the only  differences  there are three different drive versions  for the rave for first of all the hybrid  version that we're testing then there's  the two liter gasoline had a 2-liter  diesel engine  but anyone wanting all-wheel-drive will  have to go for the hybrid version  because unlike the previous generation  you can no longer combine the diesel  with all-wheel-drive and automatic  transmission Toyota is hoping that 60%  of customers will opt for the hybrid a  plus for the environment the manuals  take on the 4th generation of the Toyota  rav4 the overall concept makes a lot of  sense it drives well and as a hybrid is  even relatively green but he has two  small criticisms first he finds the  choice of dry version somewhat limited  and second the lack of visibility to the  rear the D pillar is very broad which  diminishes the drivers rear view on  target of in Fulani Cassandra versus  fellow
 

